# suite = unavailable: <reason>
#
# Optional. Only needed when one of this base's own SUPPORTED_SUITES
# (base.env) cannot back a Live image: when no package on that suite's
# archive provides the dracut modules mods/stack.sh's
# ensure_dracut_live_modules() requires (LIVE_DRACUT_MODULES there). Check
# the real archive index before writing an entry (see bases/ubuntu/live.map
# for the worked example: jammy, checked against archive.ubuntu.com) — do
# not guess. A suite genuinely fine for a Live image needs no line here, and
# a base with no such limitation at all needs no live.map file at all; this
# file only ever lists exceptions, so it never has to be kept in sync with
# SUPPORTED_SUITES by hand (tools/render_manifest.py refuses a render whose
# live.map names a suite SUPPORTED_SUITES doesn't).
#
# tools/render_manifest.py refuses, at render/--check time, a manifest that
# names a suite listed here — before a chroot ever runs. mods/stack.sh's own
# in-chroot check stays in place regardless: this file only catches a gap
# already known; that check is the backstop for one that opens up later.
#
# example (delete before use):
# jammy = unavailable: no package on jammy provides the dmsquash-live-autooverlay or overlayfs dracut module; use a newer suite instead
